Z||000000||BBBAD GT||09-17-2000||10:48 PM||||Took the V8 Fiero to a local car show, and to find out the only other Fiero there was another V8.  It turns out the guy only lives 14 miles away from me, and this is the first I've ever seen it (Its the white/yellow 85 Mercruise Fiero, real neat car, forum member too, maybe he'll reply to this).  We talked a bunch about these hybreds we have, and entered the same class, 1984+ custom.<P>At the end of the day, first place went to a 1998 Supercharged GrandPrix.  I was a little taken back as to why this car won, and also what mods were done to make it custom. It was showroom stock in appearence inside and out.  I asked the owner of the GrandPrix what has been done to it, he said:<BR> <BR>1)Intercooler<BR>2)Smaller blower pulley<BR>3)custom Eprom<BR>4)K&N Filter<P>Thats it.  Bone stock everything else.  I wasn't upset with him, just puzzled as to why he won and the new definition of 'custom'.  Oh well, you win some you lose some (in this case, I got second  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>To top off this day, I was running down to the local Taco Hell, and I pull up to a motorcycle with a 350 between his legs.  I've seen these motorcycles in big nationwide shows before, but not in our local town.  We both gave eachother the 'nice ride' nod.  <P>Normally, this all doesn't happen in the same day.  Strange.<P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">    <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||12
